Package: rthologs
Title: Gene Orthologs for Model Organisms in a Tidy Data Format
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Igor", "Dolgalev", , "igor.dolgalev@nyumc.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4451-126X"))
Description: Genomic analysis frequently involves comparisons to human or
    mouse data. This requires harmonization of gene names into the same
    gene space. The 'rthologs' R package simplifies cross-species
    conversion and mapping between gene orthologs/homologs of common model
    organisms such as human, mouse, rat, zebrafish, and fly. It supports
    gene symbols, NCBI (Entrez) IDs, and Ensembl IDs, and works offline.
    The orthologs are sourced from the Alliance of Genome Resources (AGR)
    <doi:10.1093/genetics/iyae049>.
